			<div class="content" id="post-content-4457716">
									

<p>Naming this was a decision between &quot;Paths to Desire&quot; and &quot;Paths to Fulfillment&quot;. I ended up going with the latter. Thanks to Calibri Bold and RockTeethMothEyes, respectively, for the suggestions!</p>
<p>So, big, big thanks to all my reviewers in chat: asaucedev, Kilonova, Jak/JakdragonX (x2), RockTeethMothEyes, LuciusIII, MalyceGraves, Calibri_Bold, TheMightyMcB</p>
<p>Particular thanks to asaucedev and TheMightyMcB for line-by-line specifics, and Jak for reading this twice!</p>
<p>Cerastes reviewed this in PMs! Thank you!</p>
<p>Image is from here: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diagonal_path,_Recreation_Ground,_Burley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_263086.jpg">https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diagonal_path,_Recreation_Ground,_Burley_-_geograph.org.uk_-_263086.jpg</a></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So&#8230; very bluntly, this is the modern version of how you get yourself the help of a fairy godmother. Obviously though, since these days it's kind of weird to water a stick with your tears while sitting at your mom's grave, all you gotta do is run along a pathway that defies human infrastructure.</p>
<p>Nearly all of the specific quirks (the clothes turning glowy, the feathers, dropped items staying conveniently in place - can you imagine if Prince Charming had to look for a shoe in the dark of midnight?) are nods to fairy tales.</p>
<p>Also, &quot;Marraine&quot; translates from French to &quot;godmother&quot;.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>This is something that's been sitting in my &quot;document of things I want to write someday&quot; for months. It's been awhile since I wrote something; I figured at the end of the year's a good a time as any. Here's hoping that everyone out there has someone/finds someone who will cheer them on through life, and best wishes for the upcoming new year!</p>

							</div>

								
